{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal-record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer; afterwards it may consider only listed serious or recent convictions, must make an individualized assessment, and may never consider arrests, expunged or sealed records, or juvenile adjudications.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; a provider may still ask about methamphetamine-manufacture convictions on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Director may impose a penalty not exceeding $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 depending on prior violations, and order compliance actions.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer, except that a housing provider may consider whether an applicant has ever been convicted of drug-related criminal activity for the manufacture or production of methamphetamine on the premises of federally assisted housing","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application-fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may give evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors; the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful provider appeal","requirement":"A housing provider whose appeal overturns a director's order may evict the former applicant housed under that order as grounds notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, if it gives at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units owned by the housing provider in which a former applicant resides as the result of a director's order under the act.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied premises","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Applies only where the person resides in the unit as the result of the director's order and the housing provider's appeal of the director's decision succeeds.","coverage_quotes":["if the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction"]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"then a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

